terms.medium_def:
A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Sa.9.1; 
only referred to as Zeror (צְרוֹר); 
a son of Becorath; 
father of Abiel. § grandfather of Ḳish

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.11; 
referred to as Merari or Merarite (מְרָרִי), or Merari or Merarite (מְרָרִי); 
son of Levi; 
a brother of Gershon, Kohath and Jochebed; 
father of Mahli, Mushi and Jaaziah. § the 3rd son of Levi and head of a Levitical family

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.11; 
referred to as Merari or Merarite (מְרָרִי), or Merari or Merarite (מְרָרִי); 
son of Levi; 
a brother of Gershon, Kohath and Jochebed; 
father of Mahli, Mushi and Jaaziah. § Merarites, of Marari "bitter"
descendants of Merari, the son of Levi, and members of a Levitical family

A woman living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Rut.1.2; 
referred to as Naomi (נׇעֳמִי), or Mara (מָרָא); 
wife of Elimelech; 
mother of Mahlon and Chilion. § a name that Naomi called herself due to her calamities

A location only mentioned at Amo.1.5; 
only referred to as Aven_Valley (בִּקְעָה אָ֫וֶן). § A town or region in Syria (Am 1:5)
a name used contemptuously a place of idolatrous worship

A location first mentioned at Gen.12.8; 
referred to as Bethel or Bethel (KJV= House of God) (בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל), or Bethel (KJV= Beth-el) (בֵּית הָאֱלִי), or Aven (NIV= "wickedness") (אָ֫וֶן), or Bochim (בֹּכִים), or Luz (לוּז), or El-bethel (KJV= El-beth-el) (אֵל בֵּית־אֵל). § a name used contemptuously a place of idolatrous worship
Bethel with its calf worship (Ho 10:8)

A Judge living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Jdg.6.11; 
referred to as Gideon (גִּדְעוֹן), or Jerubbaal (יְרֻבַּ֫עַל), or Jerubbesheth (יְרֻבֶּשֶׁת), or Gideon (Γεδεών); 
a son of Joash; 
father of Jether, Abimelech and Jotham. § name given to Gideon by his father when he destroyed the altar of Baal

Jonathan's son from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.4.4; 
referred to as Mephibosheth (מְפִיבֹשֶׁת), or Merib-baal (מְרִיב בַּ֫עַל), or Merib-baal (מְרִי בַעַל); 
a son of Jonathan; 
father of Micah.

A location near Kadesh-barnea first mentioned at Num.20.13; 
referred to as Meribah (מְרִיבָה), or Meribah/-kadesh (KJV= "strife in Kadesh") (מְרִיבָה קָדֵשׁ). § ♣1) a fountain at Rephidim, in the desert of Sin; so called because the Israelites murmured against God
2) the name of the water supply at Kadesh on the southern border of the promised land; the people also murmured here against God

Jonathan's son from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.4.4; 
referred to as Mephibosheth (מְפִיבֹשֶׁת), or Merib-baal (מְרִיב בַּ֫עַל), or Merib-baal (מְרִי בַעַל); 
a son of Jonathan; 
father of Micah.

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.23.29; 
only referred to as Ribai (רִיבַי); 
father of Ittai. § father of Ittai the Benjamite of Gibeah

A Judge living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Jdg.6.11; 
referred to as Gideon (גִּדְעוֹן), or Jerubbaal (יְרֻבַּ֫עַל), or Jerubbesheth (יְרֻבֶּשֶׁת), or Gideon (Γεδεών); 
a son of Joash; 
father of Jether, Abimelech and Jotham. § a variant name of Jerubbaal ) substituting the word 'shame' for the name of the pagan god 'Baal'

A man from the tribe of Simeon living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.10; 
referred to as Jachin (יָכִין), or Jachinite (יָכִינִי), or Jarib (יָרִיב); 
son of Simeon; 
a brother of Jemuel, Jamin, Ohad, Zerah and Shaul.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.11.46; 
only referred to as Jeribai (יְרִיבַי); 
son of Elnaam; 
a brother of Joshaviah. § a descendant of Elnaam and one of David's mighty warriors

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Sa.21.8; 
only referred to as Mephibosheth (מְפִיבֹשֶׁת); 
son of Saul and Rizpah; 
a brother of Armoni; 
half-brother of: Jonathan, Abinadab, Malchi-shua, Merab, Michal and Ish-bosheth.

Jonathan's son from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.4.4; 
referred to as Mephibosheth (מְפִיבֹשֶׁת), or Merib-baal (מְרִיב בַּ֫עַל), or Merib-baal (מְרִי בַעַל); 
a son of Jonathan; 
father of Micah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.10; 
only referred to as Harumaph (חֲרוּמַף); 
father of Jedaiah. § father of Jedaiah, one of the builders of the wall in Nehemiah's time

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Num.1.9; 
only referred to as Helon (חֵלֹן); 
father of Eliab. § father of Eliab of the tribe of Zebulun
